Good result,
so what the algorithm does if the the total vertices size is less than 100, 
it fall back to sequential bfs, otherwise it uses the level-synchronous parallel bfs with per-vertex candidate collection, which allows it to maintain the correct discovery order while still achieving parallelism on larger levels of the graph.
but this parallel implementation only kicks in if the current frontier level has 4 or more vertices, otherwise it processes that level sequentially to avoid overhead on small levels. This hybrid approach allows it to efficiently handle both small and large graphs while respecting the BFS discovery order.


